      "message": "\u003e You might as well call `pd_set_input_current_limit` with 1mA instead of 0 to verify the behavior.\n\nChange to call `pd_set_input_current_limit()` to 1mA, then run TEST.PD.PS.SNK.1: \nFail the test, after PS_RDY, we draw current 60-90mA (\u003e pSnkSusp 25mW)\n\nAlso try:\nWhen negotiate with adapter 20V/3.25A, calling `pd_set_input_current_limit()` to \n-\u003e 1A: the drawing current can be limited to 99XmA (without any change the current is 18xxmA)\n-\u003e 1mA or 0mA: the drawing current is 60-90mA (needs to call `typec_set_input_current_limit()`, current can be down to 1~4mA)\n\n\n \n\u003e\u003e One potential fix would be to make the charge manager ignore a source only if available voltage is 0:\n\n\u003e Can you try this? If it works, it seems like a more general and obviously correct solution.\n\nFail the test TEST.PD.PS.SNK.1, the drawing current is 60-90mA (\u003e pSnkSusp 25mW)",
