      "writtenOn": "2024-10-08T16:22:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Change to call pd_set_input_current_limit() to 1mA, then run TEST.PD.PS.SNK.1:\nFail the test, after PS_RDY, we draw current 60-90mA (\u003e pSnkSusp 25mW)\n\nWhat does \u0027chgsup\u0027 command say?\n\nSince your CL works, I think there is no minimum current limit statically enforced internally or externally. Thus, if the charge manager is working as expected, I still believe setting limit to 1 mA should make the charge manager choose the PD as a source. In other words, a call to typec_set_input_current_limit in your pd_sink_stop_drawing_current isn\u0027t needed because the charege manager selects the PD port because of the PD\u0027s priority is higher than TC\u0027s.\n\n[This](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/charge_manager.c;l\u003d683) is the code I\u0027m referring to. You might as well add printfs and see what\u0027s happening there?",
